From 2a496a67a1c94f4725fa33db61b1444d9da313b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Veronika Miticka <vmiticka@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Feb 2026 16:09:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add CSP headers to webui

Add Content-Security-Policy headers for legacy and modern web UI.

We should use permissive CSP for all the pages but modern-webui, as they
are all based on the old dojo framework, this should be revisited once
we revisit the error pages.
We really should just use setifempty and hardcode the CSP for all the
subpages. This is not the safest solution, but safe enough while not
difficult to get right.
When reviewing, note, that frame-ancestors is server-side only
directive.

Legacy UI: Extract inline scripts from index.html, reset_password.html,
and sync_otp.html into external JS files to eliminate the need for
script hash in the CSP policy.

Fixes: https://codeberg.org/freeipa/freeipa/issues/9900
Fixes: https://codeberg.org/freeipa/freeipa/issues/9901

Signed-off-by: Veronika Miticka <vmiticka@redhat.com>
